gsipper (1.0.7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix pjlib assertion ('Calling pjlib from unknown/external thread')
    crashing the app right after a recorded call ended. The
    AudioMediaRecorder ref was being dropped on the GTK main thread,
    so the SWIG-generated destructor invoked pjmedia cleanup off the
    pjsua2 worker. Both the call and recorder refs are now packaged
    into a no-op closure submitted to the worker after the 5-second
    grace period, so SWIG destructors run on a pjsua2-registered
    thread.
  * Fix AttributeError 'AudioMediaRecorder object has no attribute
    "delete"' — that method only exists on pj.Account. The recorder
    closes through Python refcount-driven destruction; the dedicated
    stop_recording() + take_recorder() now reflect that.

 -- pulpoff <noreply@pulpoff.com>  Tue, 19 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

gsipper (1.0.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Disconnect now paints the headerbar dot red immediately. The
    trunk's 200 OK to our un-REGISTER used to flap the dot back to
    yellow (Registering...). A user-disconnect latch is now consulted
    in _on_reg_state and cleared by Connect / Reconnect / any
    successful REGISTER.
  * _teardown_account_locked logs 'tearing down existing account' /
    'account torn down', and _do_configure_account logs 'new account
    created; REGISTER initiated' so the Reconnect path is auditable
    from the log.

 -- pulpoff <noreply@pulpoff.com>  Tue, 19 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

gsipper (1.0.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Settings: new "Enable messages" toggle (default off). When off,
    the Messages tab is hidden from the view switcher. Stored
    conversations are preserved; turning the toggle back on
    re-adds the tab in place. Toggling is live — no restart needed.

 -- pulpoff <noreply@pulpoff.com>  Tue, 19 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

gsipper (1.0.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Reconnect now does a real reconnect: tears down the pjsua2
    Account and rebuilds it through configure_account, so a fresh
    REGISTER actually goes on the wire. The previous
    setRegistration(True)-only path short-circuited inside PJSIP
    when the existing registration was still valid.

 -- pulpoff <noreply@pulpoff.com>  Tue, 19 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

gsipper (1.0.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Status dot becomes a Gtk.MenuButton with a state-dependent menu:
    Disconnect / Reconnect / Exit when online, Connect / Exit when
    offline. Reconnect is now a refresh REGISTER (calling
    setRegistration(True) on an already-registered account); the
    previous Disconnect-then-Reconnect pattern tripped
    pjsua2.Error because PJSIP rejects the second call while the
    un-REGISTER transaction is still settling.
  * Faster GUI startup. The 40 MB pjsua2 .so and the SipEndpoint
    singleton are imported / built on the next idle slot AFTER the
    window paints. The window, tray icon and shell-extension
    D-Bus property are visible in their initial state ("connecting"
    or "offline" depending on account configuration) from frame 1.

 -- pulpoff <noreply@pulpoff.com>  Tue, 19 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

gsipper (1.0.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Settings dialog (start minimized / run on start / record calls).
  * Call recording: WAV via PJSUA2, MP3 conversion via ffmpeg,
    in-app playback dialog with timeline and transport buttons.
  * Window X button hides to tray; SIP stays registered. Real quit
    via win.quit / Ctrl+Q / tray-extension Quit.
  * Bundle pjsua2 (built locally with pjproject 2.15) into the deb.
  * Extension metadata: shell-version 45..49 + numeric version=1.

